            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Your truck’s suspension system does more than provide a smoother ride. It plays a major role in vehicle stability, steering control, tire wear, cargo protection, and overall driver safety. When suspension components begin to wear out, small issues can quickly turn into expensive repairs and unexpected downtime. For owner-operators and fleet managers, recognizing the warning signs early can help prevent bigger problems on the road. Understanding how semi truck suspension parts work and when they need attention is one of the best ways to keep your trucks operating safely and efficiently.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-it-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Semi Truck Suspension Parts Matter",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-it-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Commercial trucks take on enormous stress every day. Heavy loads, uneven roads, long-distance driving, and stop-and-go traffic all place strain on suspension systems over time. Your truck’s suspension system helps:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-it-matters-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Absorb road shock"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Maintain tire contact with the road"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Support proper steering and handling"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Protect cargo during transport"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduce wear on other vehicle systems"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When suspension components begin failing, the effects often spread into other areas of the truck, including tires, steering, and driveline systems. That’s why routine inspections and timely truck suspension repair are so important for fleet performance and safety.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-common-parts",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Semi Truck Suspension Parts That Wear Out",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "common-parts"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-parts-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Several suspension components naturally wear down with mileage and heavy use. Frequently replaced suspension components include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-common-parts-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Shocks and struts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air springs and airbags"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Torque rods"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Bushings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Leaf springs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "U-bolts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension hangers"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Control arms"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-common-parts-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Over time, even quality semi truck suspension parts eventually need replacement due to daily wear and tear.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs Your Suspension System Needs Attention",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The earlier you catch suspension problems, the easier and less expensive repairs usually become. Here are some of the most common warning signs to watch for.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Uneven Tire Wear",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Uneven tire wear is often one of the first signs of suspension trouble. When suspension components wear out, the truck’s weight may no longer distribute evenly across the tires. You may notice:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-signs-4",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Excessive wear on one side"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cupping or scalloped tread patterns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Premature tire replacement needs"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension issues and alignment problems often go hand in hand, which is why a professional <a href=\"/blog/posts/when-to-schedule-semi-truck-alignment-near-me\">truck alignment service</a> is important when abnormal tire wear appears. Ignoring tire wear problems can increase operating costs and reduce fuel efficiency over time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Rougher Ride Quality",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If your truck suddenly feels rougher on the road, the suspension system may no longer be absorbing impact properly. Drivers often notice:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-signs-8",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Increased vibration"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Excessive bouncing"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Harsh impacts over bumps"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduced steering stability"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-9",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While some ride changes happen gradually, they should never be ignored. A rough ride can affect driver comfort, cargo protection, and vehicle handling.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-10",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Leaning or Sagging",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-11",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A truck that appears uneven while parked or loaded may indicate worn air springs, broken leaf springs, or damaged suspension supports. Leaning or sagging can place additional strain on other systems and may even affect braking performance. If you notice your truck sitting lower on one side, schedule truck suspension repair as soon as possible.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-12",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Steering Problems and Poor Handling",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-13",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Worn suspension parts often affect steering response and vehicle control. Common symptoms include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-signs-14",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Drifting while driving"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loose steering feel"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Difficulty maintaining alignment"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Excessive body roll during turns"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-15",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Poor handling not only increases driver fatigue but can also create safety risks on busy highways or during poor weather conditions.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-signs-16",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Excessive Vibrations",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-signs-17",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Not all vibrations come from tires alone. Damaged suspension components or worn driveline parts can create vibrations throughout the truck. Sometimes the issue may involve both the suspension system and driveline parts for commercial trucks working together under heavy loads. Professional diagnostics can help pinpoint the exact source before it develops into a larger repair.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-parts",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Need Reliable Semi Truck Suspension Parts?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "parts"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-parts-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Finding quality parts quickly matters when trucks need repairs. Sun State International’s parts department offers dependable OEM and aftermarket semi truck suspension parts designed to support all makes and models of semi-trucks and trailers throughout Florida.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
