                {
                  "id": "h-downtime",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Suspension Problems Lead to Downtime",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "downtime"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-downtime-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many fleet owners delay suspension repairs because the truck is still technically operational. Unfortunately, waiting too long often creates bigger and more expensive problems later. Failing suspension systems can lead to:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-downtime-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Accelerated tire wear"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Steering component damage"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Driveline strain"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake system issues"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased fuel consumption"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Unsafe driving conditions"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-downtime-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Most importantly, breakdowns create costly downtime. For trucking businesses, downtime affects scheduling, customer relationships, driver productivity, and overall profitability. That’s why many fleets prioritize preventative maintenance and reduce truck downtime services whenever possible.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventative",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventative Maintenance Helps Protect Your Fleet",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventative"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventative-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Routine inspections are one of the best ways to catch suspension issues early. During preventative maintenance, technicians can check:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-preventative-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension bushings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air suspension systems"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Shock absorbers"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Alignment settings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Driveline components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Steering performance"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tire wear patterns"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventative-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Regular inspections not only improve safety but also help extend the life of other vehicle systems. At Sun State International, our service teams work with owner-operators and fleets throughout Florida to help identify maintenance concerns before they lead to major downtime.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-keep-moving",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keep Your Trucks Riding Smoothly With Sun State International",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "keep-moving"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-keep-moving-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The longer worn components go ignored, the more strain they place on tires, steering systems, and driveline components. If your truck is showing signs of suspension wear, now is the time to have it inspected. From truck alignment service to complete suspension system repairs, Sun State International is here to help fleets and owner-operators reduce downtime and stay safely on the road. Schedule your service appointment today and let our team help keep your operation moving forward.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
